he Ozark Highlands Trail runs for more than 200 miles between Lake Fort Smith and the Buffalo National River, while forest recreation areas open up day hikes, backpacking, waterfalls, mountain biking, fishing and scenic drives.</p><p>Use OzarkRoost as the planning layer: pick a trail or water adventure, choose a nearby base, then add food, attractions and another destination.</p></article><aside class="card"><div class="stat"><b>200+ mi</b><span>Ozark Highlands Trail route</span></div><div class="stat"><b>Forest + rivers</b><span>hiking, paddling, fishing and camping</span></div><div class="stat"><b>4 seasons</b><span>each with a different Ozark personality</span></div></aside></section><div class="head"><h2>Choose your adventure</h2></div><section class="tiles"><a class="tile" href="/guides/best-hiking-ozarks"><span class="num">01 · HIKE</span><h3>Hit the trail</h3><p>Build a day hike, overnight backpacking route or section adventure around your time and ability.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-waterfalls"><span class="num">02 · WATERFALLS</span><h3>Chase a waterfall</h3><p>Spring and wet-weather trips can turn forest hollows into some of the Ozarks' best scenery.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-camping"><span class="num">03 · CAMP</span><h3>Camp out</h3><p>Choose an established campground or appropriate backcountry site and check current rules first.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-scenic-drives"><span class="num">04 · DRIVE</span><h3>Take the long way</h3><p>Wind through mountain roads, tiny communities, overlooks and trailheads.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-fishing-trips"><span class="num">05 · FISH</span><h3>Find the water</h3><p>Rivers, creeks and lakes give anglers another reason to slow down.</p></a><a class="tile" href="/guides/ozarks-weekend-getaway"><span class="num">06 · WEEKEND</span><h3>Make it a basecamp</h3><p>Book a cabin, plan two signature adventures and leave room for weather.</p></a></section><div class="head"><h2>Build the trip</h2></div><section class="plans"><article class="plan"><h3>Day trip</h3><p>One trail, one scenic stop, one great meal. Keep the route simple and flexible.</p><a href="/guides/best-hiking-ozarks">Start hiking →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Overnight</h3><p>Pair a longer trail with a campground or cabin close to your next morning's adventure.</p><a href="/listings">Find a stay →</a></article><article class="plan"><h3>Long weekend</h3><p>Connect the Highlands with Buffalo River, Mountain View or another Ozark hub.</p><a href="/destinations/buffalo-river">Add Buffalo River →</a></article></section><section class="card owner"><h2>Own an Ozark Highlands business?</h2><p>Add your cabin, outfitter, restaurant, guide service or experience to the growing destination directory.</p><a class="btn primary" href="/list-your-cabin">Claim a free founding spot →</a></section><div class="disclosure">OzarkRoost is an independent travel directory. Trail conditions, closures, water levels, regulations and access can change. Verify current information with the responsible public-land agency before traveling.</div></main></body></html>